{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.OptimalNF","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OptimalNF","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.pp_extension_not_prefix_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.pp_extension_not_prefix_closed","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L295-L324","doc":"pp crossings have d = 0: pure extension (without identity preservation)\ncannot produce a prefix-closed support unless every non-empty element\nof S already ends with k.  In particular, if S contains a non-empty\nword that does NOT end with k, then `S.map (w ↦ w ++ [k])` fails\nprefix closure.\n\n**Proof**: if `w ∈ S` with `|w| ≥ 1` and `w` does not end with `k`,\nthen `w ++ [k]` has length ≥ 2, so prefix closure requires\n`w = (w ++ [k]).dropLast ∈ S.map (v ↦ v ++ [k])`.\nBut then `w = v ++ [k]` for some `v ∈ S`, meaning `w` ends with `k`\n— contradicting our hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.IsMagic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.IsMagic","kind":"def","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L289-L289","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.magicNumbers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.magicNumbers","kind":"def","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L288-L288","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.hecke_stays_in_basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.hecke_stays_in_basis","kind":"theorem","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L278-L282","doc":"σ² = HA·σ + 1: both outputs are in the basis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.optimal_nf_characterization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.optimal_nf_characterization","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L267-L272","doc":"The standard basis has exactly A terms and none are absorbable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.optimal_nf_is_standard_basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.optimal_nf_is_standard_basis","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L255-L265","doc":"**Main Theorem**: the optimal NF of a stable nucleus is the standard basis. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:optimal-normal-form-valley","label":"thm:optimal-normal-form-valley","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/optimal-normal-form-valley.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.nf_support_prefix_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.nf_support_prefix_closed","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L218-L249","doc":"The NF support of a stable nucleus is prefix-closed.\nThis is the key Layer 2 result. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.valleyOfStability","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.valleyOfStability","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L216-L216","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.d_nonzero_preserves_prefix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.d_nonzero_preserves_prefix","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L195-L210","doc":"When d ≠ 0, multiplying by (c·σ_k + d) preserves prefix closure.\nThe d-term preserves all existing words; the c-term extends them.\nEvery extended word w++[k] has prefix w still in the support. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.multiply_standard_basis_absorbed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.multiply_standard_basis_absorbed","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L170-L189","doc":"After multiplying standardBasis n by σ_k (with k < n),\nall new words are either in the basis or absorbable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.optimal_from_prefix_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.optimal_from_prefix_closed","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L151-L164","doc":"If prefix-closed + generators bounded: non-absorbable ⊆ standardBasis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.prefix_closed_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.prefix_closed_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L141-L149","doc":"In a prefix-closed support, only length ≤ 1 words survive I₉. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.prefix_closed_absorbable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.prefix_closed_absorbable","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L133-L139","doc":"In a prefix-closed support, every word of length ≥ 2 is I₉-absorbable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.IsPrefixClosed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.IsPrefixClosed","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L130-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.cross_term_absorbable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.cross_term_absorbable","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L113-L124","doc":"Any pair [i, k] is absorbable when both [i] and [k] are in the basis.\nAdjacent: I₈. Non-adjacent: I₉ (prefix [i] present). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.standardBasis_not_absorbable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.standardBasis_not_absorbable","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L96-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.singleton_not_i9","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.singleton_not_i9","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L91-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.singleton_not_i8","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.singleton_not_i8","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L86-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.nil_not_i9","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.nil_not_i9","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L81-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.nil_not_i8","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.nil_not_i8","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L76-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.i9_absorb_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.i9_absorb_cons","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L62-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.i8_absorb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.i8_absorb","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L56-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.IsAbsorbable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.IsAbsorbable","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L52-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.IsI9Absorbable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.IsI9Absorbable","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L49-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.IsI8Absorbable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.IsI8Absorbable","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L46-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.singleton_mem_standardBasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.singleton_mem_standardBasis","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L36-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.nil_mem_standardBasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.nil_mem_standardBasis","kind":"theorem","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L31-L33","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.standardBasis_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.standardBasis_length","kind":"theorem","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L26-L28","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.standardBasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.standardBasis","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OptimalNF.lean#L22-L23","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OptimalNF.HeckeWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OptimalNF.HeckeWord","kind":"def","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d1